# Build context for the UI image (Dockerfile.ui, context `.`).
#
# `core/` is the one that matters: its `target/` directory is ~15 GB of Rust build artefacts, and
# without this line every `docker compose build ui` uploads all of it to the daemon. That is not a
# slow build, it is a full disk — it filled a 228 GB volume and failed with an I/O error. The UI
# image needs the front end and nothing else; the API has its own context under `core/`.
core

node_modules
dist
.git
.github

# Local state that must never end up in an image.
.env
.env.local
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Test and tooling output.
coverage
playwright-report
.vite
